Vendored upstream files and their local changes:

- `lib/index.js` — the upstream Host module with the package-local binary
  resolution replaced by installed-CLI discovery (`codexPath`, then `codex` on
  `PATH`), `codex --version` validation, Windows `ComSpec` handling for
  `.cmd`/`.bat` shims, the two provider instances, and the
  `codex_subagent_status` tool. The app-server protocol adapter, subprocess
  lifecycle, cancellation, and teardown code are retained from upstream.
- `lib/types/index.d.ts`, `lib/types/run.d.ts`, `lib/types/wire.d.ts` — upstream
  declarations, updated for the local config and path/import changes.
- `lib/index.d.ts` — local re-export of the vendored declarations.

The fork does not depend on the official provider package at runtime and ships
no Codex binary. It runs the Codex CLI installed on the user's machine and uses
that user's Codex configuration and authentication.
